  "limitations": [
    "Experiment only: source coordinate frame and acceleration units remain unverified. Train-only standardization does not establish SI calibration or vehicle-frame compatibility.",
    "Clock granularity is one second, with repeated timestamps and varying intervals. Seven source rows are an index-domain window, not an aligned 5-8 second feature window. Do not interpolate or claim detection latency.",
    "Only three drivers in a small shared hardware/vehicle/route population. Held-out-driver results do not establish route, device, mount or motorcycle generalization.",
    "Four publisher maneuver labels only, with unverified annotation boundaries; no ordinary-driving negative, road-impact, phone-movement or crash label. False severe events/hour cannot be measured.",
    "One predeclared split: driver 1 train, driver 2 validation, driver 3 locked test. One trailing seven-row window per task, with no cross-task windows. Never train on version-2 quarantine or synthetic-only data as field evidence.",
    "No governed Traelyx event/score mapping, calibration, severe-event claim or mobile benchmark.",
    "Reproducibility is checked within the pinned environment; cross-platform numeric identity is not promised.",
    "Retrospective audit: validation driver selected the original checkpoint; test driver was previously reported.",
    "35 calibration tasks and 39 test tasks are insufficient for population or safety calibration claims.",
    "No normal/severe truth or production event mapping: false severe events/hour remains unavailable, not zero.",
    "Disagreements are with source labels, not confirmed real driving errors or causal explanations."
  ],
